From b6bc6b6cbc71a2367e8d2e84c92ec46e535c2c23 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SteveDeFacto <5148995+SteveDeFacto@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 21:05:02 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 13/19] Let independent CLI/MCP, management and native callers
 choose the local verifier

--chain-verifier (CLI, independent mode only) and the MCP profile key chainVerifier take a
loopback verifier URL. When set, the management LeaseReader and the platform host policy
read through it (no quorum fallback after a refusal); every other independent-mode read and
every transaction still uses the explicit RPC quorum, which remains required. The
ManagementClient and NativeClient accept chainAuthority/chainVerifier and pass them to
their LeaseReader. A remote verifier URL is refused.

(cherry picked from commit 2efc4a83ec6636f875fa4523d50674bda06bcdcb)
